  "id": "Compound::DB06637 - Gene::3749",
  "verbalization": "Dalfampridine is shown to bind to Kcnc3, Kcnf1, and Kcna7, all of which are involved in the same pathway of Delayed Rectifier Potassium Channel Activity. This pathway is ultimately linked to Kcnc4, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Dalfampridine may influence Kcnc4 function. The high scores in all three paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship between Dalfampridine and the delayed rectifier potassium channels, which are critical for maintaining electrical activity in neurons. The shared involvement of these channels in the same biological process supports the idea that Dalfampridine may modulate Kcnc4 through a common mechanism, possibly by affecting the activity of the delayed rectifier potassium channels. The evidence suggests that Dalfampridine could exert a pharmacological effect on Kcnc4, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm this relationship.",
